@ 28.1.2 - Proto-Eastern Muskogean to Creek
# citation: Pogostick Man, from Booker, Karen (2005), “Muskogean Historical Phonology”. In Hardy,
# 			Heather Kay, and Janine Scancarelli, eds., Native Languages of the Southeastern United
# 			States 246 – 298
	V₁kV₂ > V₂ː / #((C)V(C))(C)_#
	V₁k > ∅ / _#
	ʃ > t͡s
	kʷ > k / #_
	kʷ > b
	S > S:[+ voice] / V_V
	h > x / _%
	V₀xV₀ > V₀ː
	# Initial vowels lost?
	x > w / a_o
	x > h
	m > ŋ / _k
	# t͡s and t alternate before k
	kl > k:[+ long]
	C:[+ long] > C:[- long]